<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Halifax, Nova Scotia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Halifax is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nova-scotia">Nova Scotia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>, on one of the world's largest natural harbours. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-cornwallis">Edward Cornwallis</a> founded it in 1749 as a British naval and military base to counter French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisbourg">Louisbourg</a>, and it became the colony's capital. A major port and naval station, it suffered the Halifax Explosion of 1917, when a munitions ship blew up in the harbour and killed about 2,000 people.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/halifax-nova-scotia.jpg" alt="Halifax, Nova Scotia" width="320" height="164" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tony Webster from Minneapolis, Minnesota · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Halifax_Harbour_Sunset_Skyline,_Nova_Scotia_(24237034620).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
